        "runId": "ada-en-3d74c885-ec18-44c9-816e-dfc3b1075fc2",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "Breakfast. Early in the morning, you’ll set off for the Bolivian border. After border checks, continue to Copacabana, a town on the shores of Lake Titicaca known for its religious shrines and lake views.\n\nA catamaran takes you across the high-altitude lake to the Island of the Sun, which Inca legends link to the origins of their civilisation. The island is home to archaeological sites and traditional settlements, and its shores look out over turquoise waters and mountain ranges.\n\nYou’ll learn about local traditions and take part in a symbolic Kallawaya ritual honouring Pachamama, or Mother Earth. In Andean culture, people thank her for life and nature’s gifts.\n\nHave lunch at a restaurant with panoramic views of Lake Titicaca, then continue across the lake to the Bolivian shore. Travel to La Paz, which lies at roughly 3,600–4,000 metres above sea level, depending on the neighbourhood.\n\nLa Paz is the seat of the Bolivian government. Its colonial buildings stand alongside modern districts and Andean markets. Stay at the 4-star Mitru or a similar hotel."
